**Issue**: #407
**Date**: 2026-09-22
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Exact-head CI-gated spec-only publication
  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: New required checks register after the spec PR opens
    Given an approved spec-only PR at head H has no reported required check
    When its required check registers pending and later succeeds
    Then publication does not merge before a fresh successful CLEAN observation
    And it merges exactly H with --match-head-commit

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Terminal required check failure
    Given a required check on the pinned PR head fails
    When publication observes terminal CI
    Then it returns actionable check failure evidence
    And it does not issue a merge

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Proven policy block and changing head
    Given successful required checks but the PR is blocked by non-CI policy
    When publication evaluates merge readiness
    Then it reports the policy blocker without merging
    But if the PR head differs from the pinned head it reports head drift instead

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Existing PR and post-merge outcome
    Given publication finds an existing PR on the issue branch
    When required CI succeeds and CLEAN is freshly reconfirmed
    Then it merges once without creating a second PR
    And the default-branch synchronization and spec-created label retain their behavior
